hannel}\", and no \"named ticket\"). The same file's unknown-value test checks the matching parser error.","kind":"file","line_end":53,"line_start":49,"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/core/repair.py"},"criterion":"`rebar store fsck --help` describes `--only` as what the command actually accepts, or the command accepts what the help describes; a test pins help text and parser behaviour together.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"_join_flag_values folds `--only <value>` and `--limit <value>` into the `=` form. fsck_cli calls it at line 356, before parsing. tests/unit/test_fsck_only_flag.py checks identical rc and stderr for both spellings, and that both spellings reach dispatch with the same values (stale-channel, 3, True). It also checks that a bare trailing --only, or one followed by a flag, still reports \"requires a value\".","kind":"file","line_end":356,"line_start":329,"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py"},"criterion":"`--only <value>` (space-separated) and `--only=<value>` behave the same.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"The reported repro `--only <id>` (space form) no longer fails with \"--only requires a value\". It now folds to `--only=<id>` and reports \"unknown --only value '<id>' (the only accepted value is 'stale-channel', with --repair)\". The help no longer claims the option takes ticket ids. Help and behaviour now agree, so the defect is resolved by making the help truthful. The ticket's own comment records this choice; it also notes that per-ticket scoping would be a feature, not this fix.","kind":"file","line_end":376,"line_start":356,"path":"src/rebar/_commands/fsck.py"},"criterion":"Bug 'store fsck --help says --only takes ticket ids; the command accepts only --only=stale-channel' is actually resolved: the reported defect no longer reproduces and expected behavior holds.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_basis":"unpinned_completion_inputs","ma